{"name":"Village Lane","hex":"#825f40","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"village","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rural habitation of size between a hamlet and a town.","A rural habitation that has a church, but no market."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/village"},{"term":"lane","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A road, street, or similar thoroughfare.","A narrow passageway between fences, walls, hedges or trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Village","blocks":[{"text":"A village is a human settlement or a residential community, larger than a hamlet but smaller than a town; some geographers describe villages as having between 500 and 2,500 inhabitants. Although villages are often located in rural areas, the term urban village is also applied to certain urban neighborhoods. Villages are normally permanent, with fixed dwellings, however, transient villages also exist. Further, the dwellings of a village are fairly close to one another, not scattered broadly over the landscape, as a dispersed settlement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG/330px-Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Village","wikidata":"Q532"},{"title":"Lane","blocks":[{"text":"In road transport, a lane is part of a roadway that is designated to be used by a single line of vehicles to control and guide drivers and reduce traffic conflicts. Most public roads (highways) have at least two lanes, one for traffic in each direction, generally separated by lane markings. On multilane roadways and busier two-lane roads, lanes are generally designated with road surface markings. Major highways often have two multi-lane roadways separated by a median."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Montague_Expressway.jpg/330px-Montague_Expressway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lane","wikidata":"Q3222002"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Veduta_di_Pacentro.jpg/500px-Veduta_di_Pacentro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Veduta_di_Pacentro.jpg/1280px-Veduta_di_Pacentro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Veduta_di_Pacentro.jpg/500px-Veduta_di_Pacentro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pacentro, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVeduta_di_Pacentro.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Stroczycy_Bielarus_2008MV04.jpg/500px-Stroczycy_Bielarus_2008MV04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Stroczycy_Bielarus_2008MV04.jpg/500px-Stroczycy_Bielarus_2008MV04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Strochitsy, Belarus, pictured 2008","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStroczycy_Bielarus_2008MV04.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Halkia%2C_Pornainen_2.jpg/500px-Halkia%2C_Pornainen_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Halkia%2C_Pornainen_2.jpg/1280px-Halkia%2C_Pornainen_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Halkia%2C_Pornainen_2.jpg/500px-Halkia%2C_Pornainen_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pornainen, Finlan